datory restart protocol. The failed initial export command did not create the file because /etc/exports.d was absent, and the later command corrected that prerequisite. No unnecessary mutations were identified. Post-executor snapshots show healthy package state and no failed services; new NFS/RPC listeners are attributable to the required NFS service, whose export is restricted to node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-05eb0b6cdf8d4a41","cmd-1c1290b5e90a4927","cmd-fa1cc135a6e5418c","cmd-0d6a319ffd754076","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service, mount, data, ownership, and write behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":[]}
